# The TLS terminator and the stack's only public entrypoint (ports 80/443).
#
# Exposure posture: Caddy forwards everything to the agent, and the agent is the
# auth boundary — every webhook validates X-Twilio-Signature against the URL
# Twilio was configured with (reconstructed from PUBLIC_BASE_URL, never trusted
# from headers), and the media WebSocket requires the secret path token. Caddy
# therefore needs no auth config of its own, and no X-Forwarded-* trust exists
# anywhere. WebSockets are proxied natively; no extra directives needed.
#
# DOMAIN must match the host in PUBLIC_BASE_URL — Twilio signs the public URL,
# and a mismatch fails every webhook's signature check. The localhost default
# lets a clean checkout boot against Caddy's internal CA with no real domain.

{$DOMAIN:localhost} {
	reverse_proxy agent:8080
}
